<title>UK: UK'S ASLEF SAYS RREA DRIVERS VOTE FOR STRIKES.</title>
<headline>UK'S ASLEF SAYS RREA DRIVERS VOTE FOR STRIKES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Associated Society of Locomotive Engineers and Firemen (ASLEF), the union which represents the country's railway workers, said on Tuesday drivers of the Regional Railways North East network had voted for a series of 24-hour strikes and a ban on overtime.</p>
<p>&quot;This vote for industrial action underlines the importance of safeguarding quality time off for train drivers,&quot; ASLEF general secretary Lew Adams said in a statement.</p>
</text>
